{
  "comment": "OMS notification relay (REV19-004). Import into Power Automate, or use as the reference for building the four cards by hand. Replace REPLACE_WITH_SHARED_SECRET with the same value set as OMS_RELAY_KEY in the gateway's Vercel environment, and authorize the shared_office365 connection as the mailbox that should send. See ../rev19-004-notification-relay.md.",
  "definition": {
    "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Logic/schemas/2016-06-01/workflowdefinition.json#",
    "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
    "parameters": {
      "$connections": { "defaultValue": {}, "type": "Object" },
      "$authentication": { "defaultValue": {}, "type": "SecureObject" }
    },
    "triggers": {
      "When_a_HTTP_request_is_received": {
        "type": "Request",
        "kind": "Http",
        "inputs": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "notificationId": { "type": "string" },
              "to": { "type": "string" },
              "recipientName": { "type": "string" },
              "subject": { "type": "string" },
              "body": { "type": "string" }
            },
            "required": ["to", "subject", "body"]
          },
          "method": "POST"
        }
      }
    },
    "actions": {
      "Check_the_shared_secret": {
        "type": "If",
        "description": "The trigger URL's sig is itself a bearer credential. This header is the second factor, so a leaked URL alone cannot send mail as the Dean.",
        "expression": {
          "and": [
            {
              "equals": [
                "@triggerOutputs()?['headers']?['X-OMS-Relay-Key']",
                "REPLACE_WITH_SHARED_SECRET"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "actions": {
          "Send_an_email_V2": {
            "type": "OpenApiConnection",
            "inputs": {
              "host": {
                "connectionName": "shared_office365",
                "operationId": "SendEmailV2",
                "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_office365"
              },
              "parameters": {
                "emailMessage/To": "@triggerBody()?['to']",
                "emailMessage/Subject": "@triggerBody()?['subject']",
                "emailMessage/Body": "@triggerBody()?['body']",
                "emailMessage/Importance": "@if(contains(coalesce(triggerBody()?['subject'], ''), 'HIGH PRIORITY'), 'High', 'Normal')",
                "emailMessage/IsHtml": false
              },
              "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
            },
            "runAfter": {}
          },
          "Respond_relayed": {
            "type": "Response",
            "kind": "Http",
            "inputs": {
              "statusCode": 200,
              "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
              "body": {
                "relayed": true,
                "notificationId": "@{coalesce(triggerBody()?['notificationId'], '')}"
              }
            },
            "runAfter": { "Send_an_email_V2": ["Succeeded"] }
          },
          "Respond_send_failed": {
            "type": "Response",
            "kind": "Http",
            "inputs": {
              "statusCode": 502,
              "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
              "body": {
                "relayed": false,
                "error": "The Office 365 connector did not accept the message.",
                "notificationId": "@{coalesce(triggerBody()?['notificationId'], '')}"
              }
            },
            "runAfter": { "Send_an_email_V2": ["Failed", "TimedOut", "Skipped"] }
          }
        },
        "else": {
          "actions": {
            "Respond_unauthorized": {
              "type": "Response",
              "kind": "Http",
              "inputs": {
                "statusCode": 401,
                "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
                "body": { "relayed": false, "error": "Bad or missing X-OMS-Relay-Key." }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "runAfter": {}
      }
    },
    "outputs": {}
  },
  "notes": [
    "IsHtml is false on purpose. createNotificationForTask builds a plain-text body joined with newlines; rendering it as HTML collapses every line break and the message arrives as one paragraph.",
    "Importance is derived from the subject rather than passed separately, because Rev 19 fixed the subject standard as the single place high priority is expressed: 'OMS | HIGH PRIORITY | Due ... | New assignment | <task> | <owner>'.",
    "The 502 branch matters: without it a failed send still returns 200 and the gateway logs nothing, so a silent mail outage looks identical to success.",
    "Phase 1 does not write status back to canonical. Relayed notifications keep reading 'pending' in OMS, and their Outlook draft link still works, so a message can be sent by hand if the relay was down. See the design note for why that is deliberate and what phase 2 should do."
  ]
}
